{title: 287 - Softly and Tenderly}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #287 • SOFTLY AND TENDERLY • 11.7.11.7}
{lyricist: Will L. Thompson}
{composer: Will L. Thompson}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 287}
{meta: tune SOFTLY AND TENDERLY}
{meta: meter 11.7.11.7}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G/D]Softly and tenderly Jesus is [C/G]calling,
[C]Calling [G]for you and for me;
[Em]At the [D]heart's [G]portals He's waiting and [C/G]watching,
[C]Watching [G]for you and for me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G/D]Come home, come home;
[D]ye who are [D7]weary [G]come home;
[G/D]earnestly, tenderly, Jesus [D/F#]is calling,
[Em]calling, O sinner, [D]come home!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G/D]Why should we tary when Jesus is [C/G]pleading,
[C]pleading [G]for you and for me?
[Em]Why should [D]we [G]linger and heed not his [C/G]mercies,
[C]mercies [G]for you and for me?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G/D]Think of the wonderful love he has [C/G]promised,
[C]promised [G]for you and for me!
[Em]Though we [D]have [G]sinned, he has mercy and [C/G]pardon,
[C]pardon [G]for you and for me.
{end_of_verse}
